== Notes ==
* {{i|Flush!}} kills Dingle instantly and causes him to leave behind 6 {{e|Dip}}s.
* If a Bomb from {{I|Butt Bombs}} goes off in the same room as Dingle, it will heal him. {{dlc+|a}} This is especially bad if Isaac happens to have {{i|No. 2}}, which causes him to drop butt bombs while firing tears.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc|a+}} Butt Bombs fired by {{I|Dr. Fetus}} and {{I|Epic Fetus}} do not heal Dingle.

== Trivia ==
* {{dlc+|a}}{{e|Dangle}} and {{e|Brownie}} are related to Dingle.{{dlc-}}
* The name 'Dingle' derives from the crude term, "dingleberry".
* Dingle was the first new boss to be shown by Edmund.<ref name="dingle">[[boisite:88344465539]]</ref>
* Dingle is referred to as male by Edmund.<ref name="dingle">[[boisite:88344465539]]</ref>
* There are three other poop monsters: Dinga, Squirt, and Dip.
** {{dlc+|a}} Two more poop monsters ({{e|Corn}} and {{e|Dank Squirt}}) and three poop bosses (Brownie, Dangle, and the {{e|Turdlings}}) were added.{{dlc-}}
** {{dlc+|r}} Four more poop monsters ({{e|Big Corn}}, {{e|Drip}}, {{e|Splurt}}, and {{e|Hardy}}) and three poop bosses ({{e|Clog}}, {{e|Colostomia}}, and {{e|Turdlet}}) were added.{{dlc-}}
* The Black Champion Version of Dingle acts slightly similar to the Dank Squirt and appears to be a "dank" or [[wikipedia:meconium|meconium]] version of Dingle.
* {{dlc|r}} Prior to ''Repentance'', all versions of Dingle could fire blood projectiles instead of just the Red Champion variant.

